Preamble

This License is source-available. It is not the Apache License, is not
affiliated with or endorsed by the Apache Software Foundation, and is not
OSI-approved open source because Section 5 limits commercial hosting.

The License keeps the broad copyright and patent grants associated with
Apache-2.0-style licensing, with four deliberate differences:

(a) it adds a GPLv2 alternative so the Work can be used in GPLv2 projects;
(b) it removes the separate NOTICE-file and per-file modification-notice
    requirements while preserving copyright and attribution notices;
(c) it requires a separate written license for Commercial Hosting; and
(d) it narrows patent termination to direct patent claims about the Work
    itself and excludes unrelated products, unrelated patents, and defensive
    counterclaims.

Sections 5 and 7 interact. The GPLv2 alternative is deliberately available
without the Commercial Hosting condition. A recipient who chooses GPLv2 can
therefore provide a hosted service without a separate commercial hosting
license, subject to GPLv2. If that outcome is unacceptable, do not rely on
the GPLv2 alternative.

This preamble is for context only and does not modify the operative terms.

1. Definitions

1.1 "Licensor" means the person or entity that makes the Work available
under this License and has authority to grant the licenses in Sections 2, 3,
and 7.

1.2 "Contributor" means Licensor and any person or entity that submits a
Contribution.

1.3 "Contribution" means any work of authorship intentionally submitted to
Licensor for inclusion in the Work, excluding Third-Party Materials.

1.4 "Work" means the software, source code, documentation, and other material
that Licensor makes available under this License, excluding Third-Party
Materials.

1.5 "Third-Party Materials" means software, data, documentation, or other
material that is not owned or controlled by Licensor and is incorporated in
or distributed with the Work, including dependencies, libraries, and assets.

1.6 "Derivative Work" means any work based on or derived from the Work and
incorporating all or part of the Work, in Source or Object form.

1.7 "Source" means the preferred form for making modifications, including
source code, build scripts, configuration, and documentation.

1.8 "Object" means any form resulting from mechanical transformation or
translation of Source, including compiled binaries, object code, and
generated artifacts.

1.9 "Modify" means to make any addition to, deletion from, or other change to
the Work, including creating a Derivative Work.

1.10 "Distribute" means to provide a copy of the Work or a Derivative Work to
a third party, in Source or Object form, including by sale, gift, or network
download. "Distribute" does not include making the Work available as a Hosted
or Managed Service, which is addressed in Section 5.

1.11 "You" means the individual or entity exercising rights under this
License, together with its Affiliates that exercise rights under this
License. "Your" has a corresponding meaning.

1.12 "Affiliate" means any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is
under common control with You.

1.13 "Control" means direct or indirect ownership of more than fifty percent
(50%) of the voting interests of an entity, or the power to direct its
management and policies, whether by contract or otherwise.

1.14 "Commercial Advantage" means any fee, subscription, advertising revenue,
data monetization, or other direct or indirect economic benefit.

1.15 "Non-Commercial" means not primarily intended for or directed toward
Commercial Advantage or monetary compensation.

1.16 "Hosted or Managed Service" means a service that provides third parties
with access to the Work or a Derivative Work over a network or as a managed
offering, including software-as-a-service, platform-as-a-service,
API-as-a-service, serverless, and managed-instance offerings.

1.17 "Commercial Hosting" has the meaning in Section 5.2.

1.18 "Licensable" means owned or controlled by a Contributor, including the
right to grant a license without payment to a third party.

1.19 "Patent Claims" means all patent claims, throughout the world, that are
Licensable by a Contributor and that are necessarily infringed by that
Contributor's Contribution alone or by the combination of that Contribution
with the Work to which it was submitted.

1.20 "GPLv2" means version 2 of the GNU General Public License, dated June
1991, as published by the Free Software Foundation. A copy is included in the
file COPYING.

