2.1 Grant. Subject to Sections 4, 5, 6, 7, and 11, Licensor grants You a
worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free copyright license to reproduce,
modify, prepare Derivative Works of, publicly display, publicly perform,
sublicense, and Distribute the Work and Derivative Works in Source or Object
form.

2.2 Contributions. Subject to the same sections, each Contributor grants You
the same copyright license for its Contributions as Licensor grants for the
Work.

2.3 Sublicenses. You may sublicense the rights in this Section 2 only under
this License or the GPLv2 alternative in Section 7.

2.4 No other rights. No copyright license is granted by implication,
estoppel, or otherwise except as expressly stated in this License.

3. Patent License

3.1 Grant. Subject to Section 3.2, each Contributor grants You a perpetual,
worldwide, non-exclusive, no-charge, royalty-free, irrevocable patent license
to make, have made, use, offer to sell, sell, import, and otherwise transfer
the Work, where the license applies only to Patent Claims.

3.2 Narrow defensive termination. If You initiate an Offensive Patent Action,
the patent license granted to You under Section 3.1 for the Work terminates
as of the date the action is filed. The copyright license in Section 2 does
not terminate under this Section.

"Offensive Patent Action" means an action or proceeding initiated by You or
Your Affiliate, other than a Defensive Counterclaim, alleging that the Work,
as made available by Licensor, or a Contribution as incorporated in the Work,
directly infringes a patent, where the accused instrumentality is the Work or
that Contribution and not a separate product or service, or Your combination
of the Work with other software or hardware.

A "Defensive Counterclaim" is a counterclaim or cross-claim alleging patent
infringement that is asserted in response to a prior action, claim, or demand
by Licensor or a Contributor against You.

An action or proceeding alleging indirect, contributory, or induced
infringement does not trigger this Section 3.2. An action or proceeding
concerning an unrelated product, an unrelated patent, or a Defensive
Counterclaim also does not trigger this Section 3.2.

3.3 No implied patent rights. No patent license is granted by implication,
estoppel, or otherwise except as expressly stated in this Section 3.

