4.6 No endorsement. You may not state or imply that Licensor endorses You or
Your Derivative Work without written permission.

5. Commercial Hosting

5.1 Condition. You may engage in Commercial Hosting only if You are the
Licensor or You have a separate written commercial hosting license from
Licensor.

5.2 Definition. "Commercial Hosting" means making the Work or a Derivative
Work available to third parties as a Hosted or Managed Service, where:

(a) the service provides users with access to a substantial set of the
    features or functionality of the Work or Derivative Work; and
(b) You receive a Commercial Advantage from the service.

A "substantial set" means a set of features that is more than a minor or
incidental part of the functionality of the Work or Derivative Work.

5.3 Exclusions. Section 5.1 does not restrict:

(a) internal use within You and Your Affiliates;
(b) personal, educational, research, or other Non-Commercial use, provided
    You do not receive a Commercial Advantage from making the Work available
    to third parties;
(c) Distributing the Work or a Derivative Work under Sections 2 and 4,
    whether for free or for a fee, if the distributed software is not
    primarily offered as a Hosted or Managed Service;
(d) providing professional services to a specific client, if the client
    receives a copy of the Work and this License and the service is not a
    general Hosted or Managed Service;
(e) using the Work as a build, test, packaging, or automation tool to produce
    software or artifacts for You or a client, where the Work is not offered
    to third parties as a Hosted or Managed Service and the primary value of
    the offering is the software or artifacts being produced; or
(f) making the Source form available, including publishing a fork, provided
    recipients comply with this License.

5.4 Violation and cure. Commercial Hosting without a separate written license
is outside the scope of the licenses granted in Sections 2 and 3. Those
licenses terminate automatically as of the first day of the violation. If You
cure the violation within thirty (30) days after receiving written notice
from Licensor, the licenses are reinstated as of the date of cure. The
reinstatement does not grant a license for the period of violation. If You
violate Section 5.1 again after reinstatement, the licenses terminate
permanently.

5.5 Separate license. A separate commercial hosting license may include
different terms. It does not change the terms of this License for copies
distributed under this License.

5.6 GPLv2 alternative. Section 7 is a deliberate alternative to this Section
5. A copy used under Section 7 is not subject to this Section 5.

