7. GPLv2 Alternative License

7.1 Alternative grant. As a separate alternative to this License, Licensor
grants You a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use,
reproduce, modify, and Distribute the Work and Derivative Works under GPLv2.
If You choose this alternative, GPLv2 governs Your copy and any Derivative
Work You distribute under it. This is a separate license grant, not an
amendment to GPLv2.

7.2 Patent grant. The patent license in Section 3.1 is also granted, on a
perpetual and irrevocable basis, to You and to recipients of a copy
distributed under GPLv2. Section 3.2 does not apply to that copy. This patent
grant is an additional permission and does not impose a further restriction
on the GPLv2 copy.

7.3 Scope. Sections 3.2, 4, and 5 do not apply to a copy that You use or
distribute under this Section 7. Section 6 continues to govern Contributions
and includes the grant made in this Section 7.

7.4 No further restrictions. If any provision of this License is construed as
a further restriction on a GPLv2 copy, that provision does not apply to that
copy.

7.5 Third-Party Materials. This Section 7 does not relicense Third-Party
Materials. Some Third-Party Materials may not be compatible with GPLv2; You
must comply with their licenses.

7.6 Trade-off. This alternative is a deliberate exception to Section 5. A
GPLv2 copy may be used to provide a Hosted or Managed Service without a
separate commercial hosting license, subject to GPLv2. If You need to prevent
that use, do not rely on this alternative.

7.7 No GPLv3. This Section 7 grants rights under GPLv2 only. It does not grant
rights under GPLv3, AGPLv3, or any later version of the GNU GPL.

